dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.animation.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.animation
start body
framing record

# animation wave: REAL binary op frame, replacing the old whole-`OpText`-line `.into_bytes()` F6
# text-as-binary shortcut (`🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`).
# `SemioAnimationMutation` is a genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed nested
# `AnimTimeline`/`AnimChannel`/`AnimKeyframe`/`SemioAnimationSnapshot` payloads — no
# `dsl::DslField` impl exists for the tagged `AnimTargetProperty`/`AnimValue` enums (hand-rolled per
# this subset's own `📸️snapshot`/`🔺️diff` convention), so the generic derive-based
# `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout doesn't apply. Handcrafted instead: `format u8`
# (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `SemioAnimationMutation` variant ordinal,
# `🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/`variant_ordinal`, 0-12, same order as `parse_op`'s
# keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own `key=value` argument payload as
# one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — the same honest boundary the sibling
# `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` uses.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
